WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.701
AI code assistants like Copilot suggest
completions, but they make mistakes,

00:00:04.781 --> 00:00:09.231
and programmers have to catch those mistakes before
they turn into bugs.

00:00:09.311 --> 00:00:14.264
One popular idea is to highlight the tokens the
model was least confident about,

00:00:14.344 --> 00:00:16.277
so a person knows where to look.

00:00:16.357 --> 00:00:23.008
This paper asks a sharp question: are those
generation probabilities actually the right thing to highlight?

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:26.405
Through a preregistered study with thirty programmers,

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:31.753
the authors compare highlighting low-probability
tokens against a new edit model that

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:35.465
instead predicts which tokens a person is likely to
change.

00:00:35.545 --> 00:00:39.868
The edit model wins on speed, precision of edits,
and user preference,

00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:43.580
showing that generation probabilities alone are not
enough.
